# Local virtualenvs. hatch builds its environments in the project root, named after the
# project (`merge-requests-monitor/`, `merge-requests-monitor-test-py3.14/` for a matrix
# env), and hides each one behind a `.gitignore` containing `*` that it writes inside the
# directory itself -- so nothing in the repository ignored them, and a checkout that
# predates the venv or a tool that only reads the repo's own ignore file was unprotected.
/merge-requests-monitor*/
/.venv*/
/venv*/
.python-version
WARP.md
